Note: ~> flow operator — multi-arg unpack + non-tuple fallthrough (TUP-10)
Note: Tests: tup ~> func calls func(tup@0, tup@1, ...); non-tuple LHS uses -> semantics
Note: Beat substitution per Wave 2 deviation note — `q` has no user-source binding,
Note: so we use Note+Note pairs (`<<C4, D4>>`) instead of the original CONTEXT block's
Note: <<C4, q>>. Same code path through the evaluator.

use "@std"

Note: ===== Test 1: 2-element tuple unpack (Note + Note) =====
proc renderHit (Note: pitch, Note: dur)
    (print (concat "hit: " (str pitch)))
end proc
Tuple<<Note, Note>> entry = <<C4, D4>>
entry ~> renderHit

Note: ===== Test 2: non-tuple fallthrough =====
proc doubleIt (Int: n)
    (mul n 2)
end proc
Int x = 5
Int r = x ~> doubleIt
(print (str r))

Note: ===== Test 3: 3-element tuple unpack =====
proc add3 (Int: a, Int: b, Int: c)
    (add a (add b c))
end proc
Tuple<<Int, Int, Int>> trip = <<1, 2, 3>>
Int sum = trip ~> add3
(print (str sum))

(print "test_unpack_flow: PASSED")
